==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[chastize]] (archaic in British English and rare in American English)

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|h₂eǵ}}
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|chastier|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|castigo|lang=la}}. See also {{l|en|chasten}}, and {{l|en|castigate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tʃæˈstaɪz/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aɪz|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|chastises|chastising|chastised}}

# To [[punish]] or [[scold]] someone.

